Package: connectivity
Title: Multi-Resolution Landscape Connectivity
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Roozbeh", family = "Valavi", email = "roozbeh.valavi@csiro.au",
           role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Calculates multi-resolution landscape connectedness, Connected
    Habitat, protected-area connectedness and the Bioclimatic Ecosystem
    Resilience Index from raster filenames or 'terra' SpatRaster objects.
    The multi-resolution method is described in Valavi, R. et al. (2026)
    <doi:10.32942/X2S68V>. Uses 'terra' for raster and vector input and output, input preparation and
    polygon analysis boundaries, and 'extendr' to call the 'connectivity-core'
    Rust numerical engine. Calculations load the analysis window into memory,
    and large rasters can be processed as aligned tiles. Also calculates exact
    fractional polygon coverage of raster cells.
    Bundled example rasters for Tasmania are licensed separately under
    CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.
